Practical retry/timeout pattern for Orbis integration (recommended):
- Client-side: 3 attempts for 500/502/503/504, incremental backoff 250ms -> 750ms -> 2000ms.
- Circuit breaker: open after 5 consecutive 5xx within 60s for a 30s cool-down.
- Idempotency: include a request-id for non-streaming calls; do NOT re-play streaming token sequences.
- Rate-limit handling: if you receive a 429, respect Retry-After where present; otherwise use an exponential backoff and apply jitter.

Sample resilience pseudo-code (Node):
async function sendWithRetries(req) {
  for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
    try {
      const res = await client.request(req);
      if (res.status === 429) {
        const retryAfter = res.headers['retry-after'] || (Math.pow(2, i) * 500 + Math.random() * 250);
        await sleep(retryAfter);
        continue;
      }
      return res;
    } catch (e) {
      if (is4xx(e)) throw e;
      await sleep(Math.pow(2, i) * 250);
    }
  }
  throw new Error('Max retries exceeded');
}

